// On iOS our BackgroundTimer falls back to plain setInterval — so when the
// JS thread is suspended (app backgrounded, screen locked, only BLE awake),
// the ping loop above stops firing entirely. The TCP socket can stay nominally
// open in the kernel for minutes while we receive zero frames, and then on
// foreground-return the user presses the camera button before the next ping
// tick runs. Result: the cloud's PHOTO_REQUEST gets written into a dead WS,
// the photo never lands, the SDK times out at 30s.
//
// The fix is to treat every transition into `active` as evidence we just
// woke up and the socket may be a zombie. We send a ping with a tighter
// deadline; if the pong does not land, we reconnect *immediately* rather
// than waiting for the next regular ping cycle.
const FOREGROUND_PROBE_PONG_TIMEOUT_MS = 2_500

